  "description": "Referees and umpires make about 40,710 dollars a year, less than the median athlete.\n\nSources:\n- BLS OEWS via api.bls.gov: Umpires, referees and other sports officials 27-2023, annual median wage, May 2025: https://api.bls.gov/publicAPI/v2/timeseries/data/OEUN000000000000027202313\n- BLS OEWS via api.bls.gov: Umpires, referees, 10th percentile: https://api.bls.gov/publicAPI/v2/timeseries/data/OEUN000000000000027202311\n- BLS OEWS via api.bls.gov: Umpires, referees, 90th percentile: https://api.bls.gov/publicAPI/v2/timeseries/data/OEUN000000000000027202315\n- BLS OEWS via api.bls.gov: Umpires, referees, employment: https://api.bls.gov/publicAPI/v2/timeseries/data/OEUN000000000000027202301\n- BLS OEWS via api.bls.gov: Athletes and sports competitors 27-2021, annual median wage: https://api.bls.gov/publicAPI/v2/timeseries/data/OEUN000000000000027202113\n\nFrom the US Bureau of Labor Statistics, Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics, May 2025 (api.bls.gov): umpires, referees and other sports officials: annual median wage $40,710, 10th percentile $26,540, 90th percentile $82,960, employment 15,780; athletes and sports competitors: annual median wage $66,710. Our math: 66,710 - 40,710 = 26,000 dollars. The pay covers officials at every level, not only pro leagues. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #referee #sports #careers #howtheymakemoney",
